    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1273">

                <pb facs="1257" n="1247" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3393/4–2449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-24T13:00:00+08:00">April 24, 1949—1
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 24—1:14 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1319. Department will, of course, appreciate that change in Navy plans (Deptel
                    733, April 23,) for second time, and at more critical moment than when
                        AAG<anchor n="66" xml:id="d1273-f1"/> announced in early December its
                    intention to withdraw, has completely scuttled emergency evacuation plan for
                    American community. I am calling a meeting of community leaders tomorrow to
                    discuss what measures, if any, civilians wish to take to assure so far as
                    possible their mutual protection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1273-f1" n="66" xml:id="d1273-f1-content">
                <p>Army Advisory Group.</p>
